 [17592186323802 #edb/ref 1074 "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $x=0.5.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(0.5,2,4)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(0.5,2)}.$ \n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂y}$ at $(0.5,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(0.5,2)} & =2+2(2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡((0.5)(2))+\\frac{1}{0.5} \\\\  & =2+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+2 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(0.5,2)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(0.5,2)}(y-2) \\\\ z-4 & =4(y-2) \\\\ z & =4y-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(0.5,2,4)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=0.5 \\\\ z &=4y-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186333100 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186333100 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186333100 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0c9a56e0-5972-5209-9d5c-ea16e82e995f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186333253 #edb/ref 1080 "-3i+\\,k" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186333253 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186333253 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1d882919-8d13-50f7-840d-8a1f45fcd980" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186333756 #edb/ref 1080 "i-2\\,k" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186333756 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186333756 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "543ab52d-1623-54f6-b166-c0e43d208801" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186333921 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186333921 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186333921 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "66686a01-21cc-56d7-951a-bacb93258c0f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186334075 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186334075 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 175921860